UID:993d1b9c-7f68-4e3a-b45d-1d85a7686f53-time.ly
DTSTAMP:20261105T055828Z
CATEGORIES;LANGUAGE=en-US:Event
CONTACT:Parks & Recreation\; 979.764.3486\; parks@cstx.gov
DESCRIPTION:<div class='ai1ec-event-avatar alignleft timely'><img src='http
 s://timelyapp-prod.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/images/54735353/Fall-Explori
 ng-History-Luncheons--Web_Facebook-Post_fRuo.jpg' /></div><p>Take a break 
 for lunch and explore the community’s past at the Exploring History Lunche
 on\, presented in partnership with the College Station Historic Preservati
 on Committee. November’s topic is “College Station: A City Founded with Pa
 rks\,” presented by Steve Beachy\, former College Station Parks and Recrea
 tion director\, and Dr. John Crompton\, professor in the Department of Rec
 reation\, Park and Tourism Sciences at Texas A&M University.</p>\n<p>The l
 uncheon will be held Wednesday\, Nov. 18\, from 11:30 a.m.–1 p.m. at the L
 arry J. Ringer Library. Attendance is free\, with lunch available for $10 
 for residents and $12 for non-residents. Lunch reservations are required b
 y Friday\, Nov. 13. A limited number of meals will be available at the doo
 r for $12.</p>\n<div class='btn' style='margin:0px\;padding:15px\;width:30
 0px\;background-color:#223d92\;text-align:center\;border-radius:5px\;color
 :#ffffff\;'><a style='background-color:transparent\;line-height:inherit\;c
 olor:#ffffff\;text-decoration-line:none\;font-weight:bold\;' href='https:/
 /txcollegestationweb.myvscloud.com/webtrac/web/search.html?Action=Start&Su
 bAction=&csrftoken=&category=EVENTS&=&primarycode=PKS-17' rel='nofollow no
 referrer noopener' target='_blank'>Reserve Your Lunch</a></div>\n<p>For mo
 re information\, contact the Parks and Recreation Administrative Office at
  979.764.3486.</p>
