UID:cd72dc5e-f72e-4079-96f0-85a146effde6-time.ly
DTSTAMP:20261105T055828Z
CATEGORIES;LANGUAGE=en-US:Event
CONTACT:Parks & Recreation\; 979.764.3486\; parks@cstx.gov
DESCRIPTION:<div class='ai1ec-event-avatar alignleft timely'><img src='http
 s://timelyapp-prod.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/images/54735353/495231297_11
 54469183390212_8100896500012261673_n_Wnx5.jpg' /></div><p>The Brazos Valle
 y Veterans Memorial Board will host its annual Veterans Day Ceremony on We
 dnesday\, Nov. 11\, at 5:30 p.m. at the American Pavilion in Veterans Park
  and Athletic Complex.</p>\n<p>The ceremony honors military veterans throu
 gh a program that includes readings\, performances\, and formal tributes. 
 It will open with the “Honor Wall Roll Call\,” a reading of the names of v
 eterans recently added to the memorial’s Wall of Honor.</p>\n<p>The progra
 m will also feature the national anthem\, a service medley recognizing Bra
 zos Valley heroes\, a rifle salute by the Texas A&M Corps of Cadets Ross V
 olunteers\, and Taps. Greg Vogel\, director of the Intelligence Studies Pr
 ogram at the Bush School and a retired Central Intelligence Agency (CIA) o
 fficer who served in the Directorate of Operations\, will deliver the keyn
 ote address.</p>\n<p>For more information\, visit <a href='https://www.bvv
 m.org/annual-events/' rel='nofollow noreferrer noopener' target='_blank'>b
 vvm.org</a>.</p>
DTSTART;TZID=CST6CDT:20261111T173000
DTEND;TZID=CST6CDT:20261111T190000
