 s://timelyapp-prod.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/images/54735353/Facebook%20E
 vent%20Images%207_KE6W.png' /></div><p class='isSelectedEnd'>Discover how 
 engineers use nature to design amazing things through hands-on exploration
  and thinking activities. Designed for ages 7–12\, the class will be held 
 Sunday\, Nov. 15\, from 2:30-4:30 p.m. at the Gary Halter Nature Center.</
 p>\n<p>Participants will explore bio-inspired engineering with experts fro
 m Texas A&M and nature educators while learning how ideas from the natural
  world can inspire engineering solutions. Dress for the outdoors\, wear cl
 osed-toe shoes and bring water.</p>\n<p>The cost is $5 for residents and $
 6 for non-residents. Registration is required.</p>\n<div class='btn' style
 ='margin:0px\;padding:15px\;width:300px\;background-color:#223d92\;text-al
 ign:center\;border-radius:5px\;color:#ffffff\;'><a style='background-color
 :transparent\;line-height:inherit\;color:#ffffff\;text-decoration-line:non
 e\;font-weight:bold\;' href='https://txcollegestationweb.myvscloud.com/web
 trac/web/search.html?Action=Start&SubAction=&csrftoken=&category=YOUTH&=&p
 rimarycode=LCN-88' rel='nofollow noreferrer noopener' target='_blank'>Rese
 rve Your Spot</a></div>\n<p>For more information\, contact the Gary Halter
  Nature Center at 979.764.6216.</p>
