DESCRIPTION:<div class='ai1ec-event-avatar alignleft timely'><img src='http
 s://timelyapp-prod.s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/images/54735353/484947580_11
 29380842563573_6618907612126856002_n_l11g.jpg' /></div><p>You don’t have t
 o travel far to make lasting memories with friends and family. Spend the n
 ight camping at Lick Creek Park on Friday\, Nov. 13. This family-friendly 
 overnight event begins at 6 p.m. Friday and concludes at 7 a.m. Saturday.<
 br /><br />Choose your adventure or join us for favorites\, such as a hot 
 dog dinner\, nature presentations\, s'mores and a night hike. Learn campin
 g basics and discover the nocturnal creatures that call Lick Creek Park ho
 me.<br /><br />Campers must bring a tent\, supplies\, snacks\, and drinks.
  Electricity is not provided\, so pack flashlights\, tent lanterns\, sleep
 ing bags\, insect repellent\, and folding chairs. Children must be accompa
 nied by an adult (18+)\, and pets are not allowed. </p>\n<p><strong>Schedu
 le of Events</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>6 p.m. • Check-in and campsite set-up
 </li>\n<li>6 p.m. • Special nature presentations\, activities\, s’mores\, 
 and games begin</li>\n<li>7 p.m. • Hot dog dinner</li>\n<li>7:30 p.m. • Ni
 ght hikes begin</li>\n<li>9 p.m. • Special nature presentations and night 
 hikes end</li>\n<li>9:45 p.m. • Activities\, s’mores\, and games end</li>
 \n<li>10 p.m. • Quiet hours begin</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The cost is $8 per perso
 n. Space is limited\, and registration closes Wednesday\, Nov. 11.</p>\n<d
 iv class='btn' style='margin:0px\;padding:15px\;width:300px\;background-co
 lor:#223d92\;text-align:center\;border-radius:5px\;color:#ffffff\;'><a sty
 le='background-color:transparent\;line-height:inherit\;color:#ffffff\;text
 -decoration-line:none\;font-weight:bold\;' href='https://txcollegestationw
 eb.myvscloud.com/webtrac/web/search.html?Action=Start&SubAction=&csrftoken
 =&category=EVENTS&=&primarycode=LCN-41' rel='nofollow noreferrer noopener'
  target='_blank'>Reserve Your Spot</a></div>\n<p>For more information\, co
 ntact the Gary Halter Nature Center at 979.764.6216.</p>
